('031f5ada-08b1-51d9-afb6-1017e7fd850a'::uuid, 6, 32, 265, 265, 'आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र समं पश्यति योऽर्जुन।

सुखं वा यदि वा दुःखं सः योगी परमो मतः।।6.32।।', 'ātmaupamyena sarvatra samaṁ paśhyati yo ’rjuna
sukhaṁ vā yadi vā duḥkhaṁ sa yogī paramo mataḥ', '[{"word":"ātma","meaning":"aupamyena—similar to oneself"},{"word":"sarvatra","meaning":"everywhere"},{"word":"samam","meaning":"equally"},{"word":"paśhyati","meaning":"see"},{"word":"yaḥ","meaning":"who"},{"word":"arjuna","meaning":"Arjun"},{"word":"sukham","meaning":"joy"},{"word":"vā","meaning":"or"},{"word":"yadi","meaning":"if"},{"word":"vā","meaning":"or"},{"word":"duḥkham","meaning":"sorrow"},{"word":"saḥ","meaning":"such"},{"word":"yogī","meaning":"a yogi"},{"word":"paramaḥ","meaning":"highest"},{"word":"mataḥ","meaning":"is considered"}]'::jsonb, 'ātma-aupamyena—similar to oneself; sarvatra—everywhere; samam—equally; paśhyati—see; yaḥ—who; arjuna—Arjun; sukham—joy; vā—or; yadi—if; vā—or; duḥkham—sorrow; saḥ—such; yogī—a yogi; paramaḥ—highest; mataḥ—is considered'),
('7238b5af-337c-51c4-b370-3db2806e8f09'::uuid, 6, 33, 266, 266, 'अर्जुन उवाच

योऽयं योगस्त्वया प्रोक्तः साम्येन मधुसूदन।

एतस्याहं न पश्यामि चञ्चलत्वात् स्थितिं स्थिराम्।।6.33।।', 'arjuna uvācha
yo ’yaṁ yogas tvayā proktaḥ sāmyena madhusūdana
etasyāhaṁ na paśhyāmi chañchalatvāt sthitiṁ sthirām', '[{"word":"arjunaḥ uvācha","meaning":"Arjun said"},{"word":"yaḥ","meaning":"which"},{"word":"ayam","meaning":"this"},{"word":"yogaḥ","meaning":"system of Yog"},{"word":"tvayā","meaning":"by you"},{"word":"proktaḥ","meaning":"described"},{"word":"sāmyena","meaning":"by equanimity"},{"word":"madhu","meaning":"sūdana—Shree Krishna, the killer of the demon named Madhu"},{"word":"etasya","meaning":"of this"},{"word":"aham","meaning":"I"},{"word":"na","meaning":"do not"},{"word":"paśhyāmi","meaning":"see"},{"word":"chañchalatvāt","meaning":"due to restlessness"},{"word":"sthitim","meaning":"situation"},{"word":"sthirām","meaning":"steady"}]'::jsonb, 'arjunaḥ uvācha—Arjun said; yaḥ—which; ayam—this; yogaḥ—system of Yog; tvayā—by you; proktaḥ—described; sāmyena—by equanimity; madhu-sūdana—Shree Krishna, the killer of the demon named Madhu; etasya—of this; aham—I; na—do not; paśhyāmi—see; chañchalatvāt—due to restlessness; sthitim—situation; sthirām—steady'),
('b04c045b-41f2-5e66-bd5b-f68952f3bf01'::uuid, 6, 34, 267, 267, 'चञ्चलं हि मनः कृष्ण प्रमाथि बलवद्दृढम्।

तस्याहं निग्रहं मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम्।।6.34।।', 'chañchalaṁ hi manaḥ kṛiṣhṇa pramāthi balavad dṛiḍham
tasyāhaṁ nigrahaṁ manye vāyor iva su-duṣhkaram', '[{"word":"chañchalam","meaning":"restless"},{"word":"hi","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"manaḥ","meaning":"mind"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇa","meaning":"Shree Krishna"},{"word":"pramāthi","meaning":"turbulent"},{"word":"bala","meaning":"vat—strong"},{"word":"dṛiḍham","meaning":"obstinate"},{"word":"tasya","meaning":"its"},{"word":"aham","meaning":"I"},{"word":"nigraham","meaning":"control"},{"word":"manye","meaning":"think"},{"word":"vāyoḥ","meaning":"of the wind"},{"word":"iva","meaning":"like"},{"word":"su","meaning":"duṣhkaram—difficult to perform"}]'::jsonb, 'chañchalam—restless; hi—certainly; manaḥ—mind; kṛiṣhṇa—Shree Krishna; pramāthi—turbulent; bala-vat—strong; dṛiḍham—obstinate; tasya—its; aham—I; nigraham—control; manye—think; vāyoḥ—of the wind; iva—like; su-duṣhkaram—difficult to perform'),
('5f42b2da-ef86-5863-a7cf-d621adb0f4cf'::uuid, 6, 35, 268, 268, 'श्री भगवानुवाच

असंशयं महाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलं।

अभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते।।6.35।।', 'śhrī bhagavān uvācha
asanśhayaṁ mahā-bāho mano durnigrahaṁ chalam
abhyāsena tu kaunteya vairāgyeṇa cha gṛihyate', '[{"word":"śhrī","meaning":"bhagavān uvācha—Lord Krishna said"},{"word":"asanśhayam","meaning":"undoubtedly"},{"word":"mahā","meaning":"bāho—mighty-armed one"},{"word":"manaḥ","meaning":"the mind"},{"word":"durnigraham","meaning":"difficult to restrain"},{"word":"chalam","meaning":"restless"},{"word":"abhyāsena","meaning":"by practice"},{"word":"tu","meaning":"but"},{"word":"kaunteya","meaning":"Arjun, the son of Kunti"},{"word":"vairāgyeṇa","meaning":"by detachment"},{"word":"cha","meaning":"and"},{"word":"gṛihyate","meaning":"can be controlled"}]'::jsonb, 'śhrī-bhagavān uvācha—Lord Krishna said; asanśhayam—undoubtedly; mahā-bāho—mighty-armed one; manaḥ—the mind; durnigraham—difficult to restrain; chalam—restless; abhyāsena—by practice; tu—but; kaunteya—Arjun, the son of Kunti; vairāgyeṇa—by detachment; cha—and; gṛihyate—can be controlled'),
('a489f5bc-cb32-598d-a09f-e43fb4b03902'::uuid, 6, 36, 269, 269, 'असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः।

वश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः।।6.36।।', 'asaṅyatātmanā yogo duṣhprāpa iti me matiḥ
vaśhyātmanā tu yatatā śhakyo ’vāptum upāyataḥ', '[{"word":"asanyata","meaning":"ātmanā—one whose mind is unbridled"},{"word":"yogaḥ","meaning":"Yog"},{"word":"duṣhprāpaḥ","meaning":"difficult to attain"},{"word":"iti","meaning":"thus"},{"word":"me","meaning":"my"},{"word":"matiḥ","meaning":"opinion"},{"word":"vaśhya","meaning":"ātmanā—by one whose mind is controlled"},{"word":"tu","meaning":"but"},{"word":"yatatā","meaning":"one who strives"},{"word":"śhakyaḥ","meaning":"possible"},{"word":"avāptum","meaning":"to achieve"},{"word":"upāyataḥ","meaning":"by right means"}]'::jsonb, 'asanyata-ātmanā—one whose mind is unbridled; yogaḥ—Yog; duṣhprāpaḥ—difficult to attain; iti—thus; me—my; matiḥ—opinion; vaśhya-ātmanā—by one whose mind is controlled; tu—but; yatatā—one who strives; śhakyaḥ—possible; avāptum—to achieve; upāyataḥ—by right means'),
('ce61bf06-b5d5-52b4-ac03-d3a7ba994502'::uuid, 6, 37, 270, 270, 'अर्जुन उवाच

अयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगाच्चलितमानसः।

अप्राप्य योगसंसिद्धिं कां गतिं कृष्ण गच्छति।।6.37।।', 'arjuna uvācha
ayatiḥ śhraddhayopeto yogāch chalita-mānasaḥ
aprāpya yoga-sansiddhiṁ kāṅ gatiṁ kṛiṣhṇa gachchhati', '[{"word":"arjunaḥ uvācha","meaning":"Arjun said"},{"word":"ayatiḥ","meaning":"lax"},{"word":"śhraddhayā","meaning":"with faith"},{"word":"upetaḥ","meaning":"possessed"},{"word":"yogāt","meaning":"from Yog"},{"word":"chalita","meaning":"mānasaḥ—whose mind becomes deviated"},{"word":"aprāpya","meaning":"failing to attain"},{"word":"yoga","meaning":"sansiddhim—the highest perfection in yog"},{"word":"kām","meaning":"which"},{"word":"gatim","meaning":"destination"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇa","meaning":"Shree Krishna"},{"word":"gachchhati","meaning":"goes"}]'::jsonb, 'arjunaḥ uvācha—Arjun said; ayatiḥ—lax; śhraddhayā—with faith; upetaḥ—possessed; yogāt—from Yog; chalita-mānasaḥ—whose mind becomes deviated; aprāpya—failing to attain; yoga-sansiddhim—the highest perfection in yog; kām—which; gatim—destination; kṛiṣhṇa—Shree Krishna; gachchhati—goes'),
('302e1229-4854-50d2-a71b-4cf3ec09afc2'::uuid, 6, 38, 271, 271, 'कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टश्छिन्नाभ्रमिव नश्यति।

अप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि।।6.38।।', 'kachchin nobhaya-vibhraṣhṭaśh chhinnābhram iva naśhyati
apratiṣhṭho mahā-bāho vimūḍho brahmaṇaḥ pathi', '[{"word":"kachchit","meaning":"whether"},{"word":"na","meaning":"not"},{"word":"ubhaya","meaning":"both"},{"word":"vibhraṣhṭaḥ","meaning":"deviated from"},{"word":"chhinna","meaning":"broken"},{"word":"abhram","meaning":"cloud"},{"word":"iva","meaning":"like"},{"word":"naśhyati","meaning":"perishes"},{"word":"apratiṣhṭhaḥ","meaning":"without any support"},{"word":"mahā","meaning":"bāho—mighty-armed Krishna"},{"word":"vimūḍhaḥ","meaning":"bewildered"},{"word":"brahmaṇaḥ","meaning":"of God-realization"},{"word":"pathi","meaning":"one on the path"}]'::jsonb, 'kachchit—whether; na—not; ubhaya—both; vibhraṣhṭaḥ—deviated from; chhinna—broken; abhram—cloud; iva—like; naśhyati—perishes; apratiṣhṭhaḥ—without any support; mahā-bāho—mighty-armed Krishna; vimūḍhaḥ—bewildered; brahmaṇaḥ—of God-realization; pathi—one on the path'),
('ace846c5-c503-58d6-85f6-aff050afda32'::uuid, 6, 39, 272, 272, 'एतन्मे संशयं कृष्ण छेत्तुमर्हस्यशेषतः।

त्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते।।6.39।।', 'etan me sanśhayaṁ kṛiṣhṇa chhettum arhasyaśheṣhataḥ
tvad-anyaḥ sanśhayasyāsya chhettā na hyupapadyate', '[{"word":"etat","meaning":"this"},{"word":"me","meaning":"my"},{"word":"sanśhayam","meaning":"doubt"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇa","meaning":"Krishna"},{"word":"chhettum","meaning":"to dispel"},{"word":"arhasi","meaning":"you can"},{"word":"aśheṣhataḥ","meaning":"completely"},{"word":"tvat","meaning":"than you"},{"word":"anyaḥ","meaning":"other"},{"word":"sanśhayasya","meaning":"of doubt"},{"word":"asya","meaning":"this"},{"word":"chhettā","meaning":"a dispeller"},{"word":"na","meaning":"never"},{"word":"hi","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"upapadyate","meaning":"is fit"}]'::jsonb, 'etat—this; me—my; sanśhayam—doubt; kṛiṣhṇa—Krishna; chhettum—to dispel; arhasi—you can; aśheṣhataḥ—completely; tvat—than you; anyaḥ—other; sanśhayasya—of doubt; asya—this; chhettā—a dispeller; na—never; hi—certainly; upapadyate—is fit'),
('ca921481-2feb-532d-b50e-d9aa96359701'::uuid, 6, 40, 273, 273, 'श्री भगवानुवाच

पार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते।

नहि कल्याणकृत्कश्िचद्दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति।।6.40।।', 'śhrī bhagavān uvācha
pārtha naiveha nāmutra vināśhas tasya vidyate
na hi kalyāṇa-kṛit kaśhchid durgatiṁ tāta gachchhati', '[{"word":"śhrī","meaning":"bhagavān uvācha—the Supreme Lord said"},{"word":"pārtha","meaning":"Arjun, the son of Pritha"},{"word":"na eva","meaning":"never"},{"word":"iha","meaning":"in this world"},{"word":"na","meaning":"never"},{"word":"amutra","meaning":"in the next world"},{"word":"vināśhaḥ","meaning":"destruction"},{"word":"tasya","meaning":"his"},{"word":"vidyate","meaning":"exists"},{"word":"na","meaning":"never"},{"word":"hi","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"kalyāṇa","meaning":"kṛit—one who strives for God-realization"},{"word":"kaśhchit","meaning":"anyone"},{"word":"durgatim","meaning":"evil destination"},{"word":"tāta","meaning":"my friend"},{"word":"gachchhati","meaning":"goes"}]'::jsonb, 'śhrī-bhagavān uvācha—the Supreme Lord said; pārtha—Arjun, the son of Pritha; na eva—never; iha—in this world; na—never; amutra—in the next world; vināśhaḥ—destruction; tasya—his; vidyate—exists; na—never; hi—certainly; kalyāṇa-kṛit—one who strives for God-realization; kaśhchit—anyone; durgatim—evil destination; tāta—my friend; gachchhati—goes'),
('d6064d04-1043-5b8c-a002-06280cff8981'::uuid, 6, 41, 274, 274, 'प्राप्य पुण्यकृतां लोकानुषित्वा शाश्वतीः समाः।

